		description=Changes `CACHE_VERSION` on every change to the app shell, most recently to add the headset media-key control (7).
		build=One constant.
		evidence=The service worker's activate handler deletes every cache whose key is not the current `CACHE_VERSION` or `BOOKS_CACHE`, so this bump is what makes 6.1 reach existing installs.
		code=|
			- [`CACHE_VERSION`](../../../../public/sw.js){change=5f0d08e..b6b8933 show=lines lines=4:4}
s7: 7 <composition>
	why=Bluetooth and wired headset keys reach whichever app the system's media-button routing currently points at, and it does not point at Codexa on its own just because the page is speaking.
	build=`ttsSessionState` (2) updates an Android `MediaSession` whose playback state mirrors the read-aloud session (4.5); the session requests audio focus while playing and plays a short silent track so media-button routing stays on this app between utterances (`TextToSpeech` audio plays in the engine's own process, not this app's); the session's callbacks call back into the page, where `window.__codexaTtsMedia` routes each action to the controller (4).
	evidence=The user confirmed on a device that a Bluetooth headset's play/pause buttons pause and resume reading.
