	n7_1: 7.1 Keep a MediaSession in step with the read-aloud session <leaf>
		why=A `MediaSession` that is not marked active, or whose `PlaybackState` disagrees with reality, does not reliably receive headset key events and shows a wrong play/pause icon wherever the state is surfaced.
		description=Creates the session lazily on first use, with a callback that maps each of its five actions to `sendTtsMedia` (7.4); sets its `PlaybackState` to `STATE_PLAYING`/`STATE_PAUSED` and marks it active; when the read-aloud session is no longer active, marks the session inactive instead of destroying it.
		build=`updateTtsMediaSession(active, playing)` is called from `ttsSessionState` (2.8), itself called from `androidEngine.session` (3.1) through `emit()` (4.5).
		invariant=(c) Media keys reach Codexa while a read-aloud session is active: the session's `isActive` flag and its `PlaybackState.STATE_PLAYING`/`STATE_PAUSED` value are set from the exact same `active`/`playing` pair the controller (4.1) emits, on every state change.
		evidence=The user confirmed on device that Bluetooth play/pause reach the app while reading; this was not exercised by an automated test.
		code=|
